    "body": " Each reader needs a distinct IPv4 address. All readers can listen on port 8443. A new reader using the standard Automatic profile tries DHCP and can use IPv4 link-local on an isolated switch. An existing saved Static profile survives power loss and firmware updates. \n     IPv4 mode  Reader  Deployment      Automatic   dhcp=true   A router or DHCP server provides a lease. Without one, the reader checks for conflicts and selects a  169.254.x.x/16  address. Leave the PC adapter on automatic addressing on an isolated switch.    DHCP reservation   dhcp=true   Reserve the reader MAC on the DHCP server. Use when managed installations need stable reader endpoints with centrally maintained settings.    Static IP   dhcp=false   Use a unique, unused address on the same subnet as the host when an installation requires fixed endpoints. Coordinate with the site DHCP administrator.     \n With an active connection, read  network.get  or select  Connection → Ethernet configuration → Read network profile  to see the effective address and MAC. A saved network profile takes effect after a restart. \n   Optional setup for an isolated switch   \n Moving between networks: leave  Automatic (DHCP / Link-local)  enabled. When changing the uplink without dropping the reader’s Ethernet link, its current DHCP lease can remain active until renewal or expiry. Search again and verify the same board ID after the address changes. "
