    "title": "Bounded inventory example",
    "href": "sdk.html#scan",
    "body": " The packaged ReadTags sample takes one argument: an Ethernet address or the application serial port. Its tag callback runs in the receive loop and must return promptly. \n  MaxDurationMs  bounds the inventory session. Select  epc ,  epc_tid  or  tid  according to the capabilities in the hello response. \n   C#  Copy    using Ndn5030.Client;\n\nif (args.Length != 1) throw new ArgumentException(\"Usage: ReadTags <IP[:port] | COM | /dev/port>\");\nstring address = args[0];\nbool usb = address.StartsWith(\"/dev/\") ||\n           (address.StartsWith(\"COM\", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) && int.TryParse(address.AsSpan(3), out _));\nawait using var reader = usb ? ReaderClient.FromUsb(address) : ReaderClient.FromEthernet(address);\nvar hello = await reader.ConnectAsync();\nvar config = await reader.GetReaderConfigurationAsync();\nConsole.WriteLine($\"{hello.BoardId}, firmware {hello.Firmware}, ceiling {config.PowerLimitDbm} dBm\");\nusing var stop = new CancellationTokenSource();\nConsole.CancelKeyPress += (_, e) => { e.Cancel = true; stop.Cancel(); };\nvar request = new InventoryRequest(Guid.NewGuid(), [1, 2, 3, 4], MaxDurationMs: 5000) { Data = \"epc_tid\" };\nvar result = await reader.ScanAsync(request,\n    tag => Console.WriteLine($\"ANT{tag.Antenna}   {tag.EpcHex}   {tag.TidHex}\"), stop.Token);\nConsole.WriteLine($\"{result.Session.Reason}   {result.ReceivedCount}/{result.Session.LastSeq}   complete={result.DataComplete}\");\nawait reader.ReleaseLeaseAsync();   \n   Note.  A reader serves one controller at a time. Select  Disconnect  in Reader Management Console before you run the example on the same reader.  \n   PowerShell  Copy    dotnet run -- 192.168.77.2\ndotnet run -- COM7   \n  ScanAsync  acquires the lease, starts inventory, receives the tag notifications and, at the end, checks that it received every sequence number up to the last one the reader reported. Cancelling the token you pass to it sends Stop for that scan; the call still returns the final result.  ReceivedCount  counts observations;  DataComplete  requires a successful terminal result, no sequence gaps, zero reported drops and zero input errors. "
